y while preserving quality. Use when the user mentions too bold, too loud, overwhelming, aggressive, garish, or wants a calmer, more refined aesthetic.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/quieter/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ralph</name>\n    <description>Convert PRDs to prd.json format for the Ralph autonomous agent system. Use when you have an existing PRD and need to convert it to Ralph&apos;s JSON format. Triggers on: convert this prd, turn this into ralph format, create prd.json from this, ralph json.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/ralph/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>roast</name>\n    <description>Adversarial cross-model review in which a finder proposes defects and an independent verifier checks each claim against the code. Use after a coherent, non-trivial code or prose change, before declaring the work complete, or when the operator asks for a Roast review.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/roast/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>shape</name>\n    <description>Plan the UX and UI for a feature before writing code. Runs a structured discovery interview, then produces a design brief that guides implementation. Use during the planning phase to establish design direction, constraints, and strategy before any code is written.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/shape/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>brainstorming</name>\n    <description>You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/superpowers/brainstorming/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>dispatching-parallel-agents</name>\n    <description>Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared