be completed honestly, leave it unchecked and record what blocked you in your notes file.\n- Do NOT read or modify files outside your current directory (the worktree).\n- Do NOT run git push.\n- Commit after each checklist item, and make sure everything is committed when finished, except your notes file.\n- Keep notes for this attempt in `.redeye/notes.md` (create the directory). Update it after each checklist item and as soon as you hit a blocker, not only at the end. Record what you implemented, files changed, how you read any vague acceptance criteria, what blocked you, and anything the next attempt at this ticket should know. Never commit, git add, or delete this file; the orchestrator collects it.\n- After completing each checklist item in the ticket, print a line: [x] <item text> (matching the checklist text exactly).\n- Before your final commit, record reusable learnings in the nearest AGENTS.md (in or above the directories you modified; prefer that over the repo root). Good additions: module conventions, gotchas, files that must change together, how to test that area, environment requirements. Do NOT add ticket-specific details or temporary debugging notes. Only write when you have knowledge that would help future work in that directory. Reusable patterns go in AGENTS.md; anything specific to this ticket goes in your notes file.\n\n</file>\n"}],"timestamp":1795205182061}}
